  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between Oblonganoside C and NCI-N87 through a series of molecular interactions involving Ent-Gloeosteretriol. The drug Oblonganoside C is predicted to target multiple proteins, including Serine/threonine-protein kinase ICK, Casein kinase I isoform alpha, and Macrophage colony-stimulating factor 1 receptor, all of which are targets of Ent-Gloeosteretriol. Ent-Gloeosteretriol, in turn, is predicted to interact with NCI-N87, indicating a possible pathway through which Oblonganoside C may influence NCI-N87. The scores from the three paths, ranging from 0.6302 to 0.6665, suggest a consistent but variable level of confidence in this relationship. The evidence highlights the role of Ent-Gloeosteretriol as a central mediator in the interaction network, with Oblonganoside C acting as a modulator of its downstream targets. The integration of these pathways underscores the complexity of the molecular interactions, emphasizing the need for further experimental validation to confirm the biological relevance of these predictions."
